Z||000000||Mickey_Moose||08-31-2001||07:25 PM||||Anyone out there willing to help out a poor sap up here in Canada?<P>The situation is this: no one up here can seem to get their hands on a set for me. Which leaves me to buying them from the US, not a problem except that no one that has them (ie. Autozone.com) will not ship to Canada. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>What I need is someone to get a pair for me, and mail them to me, I will pay all costs of them - just need to get them here. Anyone want to give me a hand?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Tim||||reg||5
Z||000001||Elenor84||08-31-2001||07:44 PM||||Hey tim...saw the post and I just knew it was u...sorry if I got your hopes up.  Good luck man!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||b52buf||08-31-2001||09:07 PM||||Mickey-- Try going to a bearing supply store.<BR>I'm sure Edmonton has at least one. Take your old bearing with you as they will need the number on the bearing and race. Bearings are pretty much made to a world wide standard, a number xxxxxxx is the same bearing where ever you buy it,as long as the number is the same. Check your phone book for bearing supply stores.<BR>GOOD LUCK<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000003||Cooter||08-31-2001||10:02 PM||||Only one problem with that- the 88's use a bearing/hub assembly similiar to front wheel drive cars. They are not serviceable with replacement bearings.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mickey_Moose||09-01-2001||10:40 AM||||I have tried every parts and bearing dealer in western Canada. I even have part numbers from several different makers, no one has them and no one can (is are willing to) order them in (the Timkin are still being made). There are a few places in the US that have other brands in stock, but no one will ship them to Canada (well that is not true, I have found one place that can still get AC Delco bearings, but they will cost me close to $600 Canadian to get them here - will use them only as the LAST resort).<P>I am looking at getting them from Autozone (Timkin make) as they are a reasonable price. Just they won't ship to Canada (and I talked to them directly)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>thanks<BR>Tim<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wannabe||09-01-2001||01:42 PM||||I didn't think it was possible to replace the bearings in the '88 front hub assembly, but rather, that it was supposed to be replaced as a whole. I'd be interested to know how you  would do this. It's also surprising to hear that you can't get a particular bearing in Canada. Most of the major manufaturers are well distributed throughout North America.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mickey_Moose||09-01-2001||05:20 PM||||well when I talk about the bearings I mean the whole hub unit - once I get some new ones, I am going to rip apart the old ones and see if it is possible to rebuild them. I did have a quick look some time ago, and it looks like it maybe possible to replace the bearings inside, but will have to get it apart and take some measurements, but did not want to do that till I have some others to replace my old ones with (in case they do not go back together properly).<P>Once I find out if they can be redone will post here with part numbers and such...<P>till then...<P>Tim<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Master_Sushi||09-01-2001||05:34 PM||||I didn't think they made the bearing/hub assembly for 88s anymore. I need to replace one on my coupe last year. I tried everywhere and couldn't fine one. Ended up getting a used one off the forum.<P>Good Luck<P>------------------<BR>88 Fiero Coupe...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mesopotamis_1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000008||Wannabe||09-01-2001||07:50 PM||||The other alternative is to buy a set of Held's drop spindles that use the same hub as the rears.||||reg||1
Z||000009||qwikgta||09-01-2001||11:28 PM||||I see this kind of post from time to time, I have an 88 and im sure that soon enough I will also need these parts.  THe question I have is, will any other GM parts fit the front end.  I will except changing my bolt pattern to 5x115 or what ever.  If the bearings are so hard to get and expensive why not look at some other GM parts that will work.  In 10-15 years we may not be able to find anyone makeing this bearing.  <P>Just my $.02<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Mickey_Moose||09-02-2001||11:05 AM||||I personally have tried, gone through a list of part numbers and cars in wreakers trying to find something that could be made to work...and what I have found was this, there is nothing that matches the size (bearing housing are bigger), and the one that may fit the mounting method is differnet, usually uses a 4 bolt pattern vs the 3 that is on the original part.<P>Future &gt;&gt; that is why I will be looking to try to rebuild my old ones once the new ones arrive - of which a kind soul has offered to help me out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Tim||||reg||1
Z||000011||Wannabe||09-02-2001||11:19 AM||||Wilwood makes replacement aluminum hubs - I wonder what chance one of them might fit???||||reg||1
